                <pb facs="0662" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.24/9</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Weeks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic">September 6,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">ASW 400.703</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to
                    acknowledge receipt of your letter of August 27, 1921, with its enclosure from
                    the Nicaraguan Minister regarding the purchase of— <list>
                        <item>5,000 rifles;</item>
                        <item>3,000,000 cartridges for same;</item>
                        <item>25 machine guns;</item>
                        <item>250,000 rounds of ammunition for machine guns</item>
                        <item>2 military aeroplanes, with their regulation supply of ammunition and
                            indispensable spare parts.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>The War Department at the present time is in a position to negotiate a sale of
                    all of the above mentioned equipment to the Nicaraguan Government except the
                    5,000 rifles. The availability of the rifles for sale will be determined at a
                    later date, but, undoubtedly, before the negotiations for the purchase of the
                    other material are concluded.</p>
                <p>It is understood, of course, that this sale is sanctioned by the State
                    Department.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Weeks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
